g Kong and Macao provisions in Chapter 59","summary":"Chapter 59 supports Hong Kong’s established international roles, the Northern Metropolis and deeper cooperation with the Mainland. It also calls for measures that facilitate residents’ development and daily life.","mechanisms":["Hong Kong’s international roles","Cross-boundary cooperation","Development and daily life"],"question":"How are national priorities translated into specific rights, services and local arrangements?","limit":"These are planning commitments. The chapter alone cannot establish delivery, take-up or social outcomes.","url":"https://www.12371.cn/2026/03/13/ARTI1773410307876581.shtml","sourceLabel":"National outline · Chapter 59 · Chinese","region":"hk"},{"id":"hk-plan-2026","year":"2026–30","date":"16 September 2026","title":"Hong Kong’s first Five-Year Plan","kind":"HKSAR development plan","scope":"Part 4, Chapter 14: Greater Bay Area development","summary":"The plan connects infrastructure, alignment of rules, and cooperation in health, elderly care, sport and culture. Its vocabulary distinguishes “hard connectivity”, “soft connectivity” and “connectivity of hearts”.","mechanisms":["Infrastructure","Rules and mechanisms","Cooperation among residents"],"question":"Who can use these arrangements, and what evidence would show that they improve everyday life?","limit":"The social dimension is already in official strategy. Whether intended users benefit remains an implementation and evaluation question.","url":"https://www.info.gov.hk/gia/general/202609/16/P2026091600197.htm","sourceLabel":"Official plan · Chapter 14","secondUrl":"https://www.info.gov.hk/gia/general/202609/16/P2026091600338.htm","secondLabel":"Announcement and indicator framework","region":"hk"},{"id":"jssez-2025","year":"2025","date":"Agreement exchanged 7 January 2025","title":"Johor–Singapore Special Economic Zone","kind":"Bilateral economic agreement","scope":"Designated areas in Johor; cooperation with Singapore","summary":"The agreement links investment promotion with movement of goods and people, business facilitation and skills cooperation. Its designated economic geography lies in Johor.","mechanisms":["Investment and business","Goods and people","Skills cooperation"],"question":"Which firms, workers and existing residents gain access to the opportunities being created?","limit":"The economic zone and the RTS rail link are separate initiatives. Agreement objectives are not measured effects.","url":"https://www.edb.gov.sg/en/about-edb/media-releases-publications/agreement-between-singapore-and-malaysia-and-the-johor-singapore-special-economic-zone.html","sourceLabel":"MTI agreement factsheet via EDB","region":"sg"},{"id":"rts-2026","year":"2026","date":"Project update · 2 October 2026","title":"RTS Link: a separate rail project","kind":"Transport delivery update","scope":"Woodlands North ↔ Bukit Chagar","summary":"The two-station rail link connects Singapore and Johor Bahru. Passenger service is targeted for February 2027, subject to independent safety certification and final regulatory approvals.","mechanisms":["Two rail termini","Testing and certification","Regulatory approvals"],"question":"Once service begins, how do actual journeys and household choices compare with forecasts?","limit":"This is a service target, not a confirmed opening or evidence of realised travel, spending or wellbeing effects.","url":"https://www.lta.gov.sg/content/ltagov/en/newsroom/2026/10/news-releases/grantors-informed-rts-link-service-targeted-feb-2027.html","sourceLabel":"LTA / Malaysia MOT joint release","secondUrl":"https://www.lta.gov.sg/content/ltagov/en/upcoming_projects/rail_expansion/JB-Singapore_RTS_link.html","secondLabel":"Project geography and termini","region":"sg"}]}
